---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import PageClose from '../components/PageClose.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/site';
const article = {
 title: 'Article template example | Servo ICT',
 headline: 'What to prepare for a website project',
 description: 'An example of a practical advice article, with a summary, contents, readable body and a relevant next step.',
 canonicalPath: '/style-guide/article/',
 topic: 'Development preview / article template',
 author: 'Servo ICT',
 publishedAt: new Date('2026-09-19'),
 readingTime: 2,
 image: '/images/pages/advice-desk.webp',
 imageAlt: 'Illustrative business desk with a laptop and notes',
 headings: [{slug:'business-details',text:'Start with the business details'},{slug:'materials',text:'Gather what you already have'},{slug:'next-step',text:'Agree the next step'}],
};
---
<ArticleLayout {...article}>
 <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
 <p><a href={sitePath('/style-guide/#templates')}>Back to the template library</a></p>
 <p>This development example shows how an article uses the shared layout. The title, introduction, image and metadata come from one data object. The content below is passed through the body slot.</p>
 <h2 id="business-details">Start with the business details</h2>
 <p>Write down what the business does, who it helps and where it works. Rough notes are useful. Decide what a visitor should be able to do after reading the page.</p>
 <ul><li>Understand the services you offer.</li><li>Find the area you cover and how to contact you.</li><li>Take a clear next step, such as starting an enquiry.</li></ul>
 <h2 id="materials">Gather what you already have</h2>
 <p>A small checklist is often enough to make the first conversation useful.</p>
 <table><caption>Material to bring to the first conversation</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Material</th><th scope="col">What helps</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Business facts</th><td>Services, opening hours and contact details.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Images</th><td>Photos you own or have permission to publish.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Existing website</th><td>Its address and a list of what needs to change.</td></tr></tbody></table>
 <h3>Keep access details separate</h3>
 <p>Describe the accounts involved without including passwords or recovery codes in your enquiry.</p>
 <h2 id="next-step">Agree the next step</h2>
 <p>Use the initial conversation to establish fit, scope and responsibilities. Confirm timing and cost before starting work.</p>
 <Fragment slot="after-article"><PageClose eyebrow="Your next step" title="Tell us what you have in mind." copy="We can help turn rough notes into a clear website scope." action="Explore website help" href={sitePath('/websites/')} theme="light" compact /></Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
